### Description

### Device description
- **Product ID:** tlgl293mqmtdwonv
- **Category:** rs
- **Device Type:** Water level controller / liquid level sensor with temperature monitoring

### Problem description
The Tuya water level controller (`tlgl293mqmtdwonv`) is incorrectly categorized as a climate/thermostat device (`category: rs`). 

The standard DPs (1–3) map to temperature values, while all water level monitoring and alarm properties reside on manufacturer-specific DPs (101–119), including:
- DP 102 (`WATERLEVEL`): Water level value
- DP 103 (`DOWNLEVEL`): Lower level threshold
- DP 104 (`UPLEVEL`): Upper level threshold
- DP 105 (`MWSWITCH`): Manual/water switch
- DP 106 (`WLALARM`): Water level alarm
- DP 110 (`DJSTATUS`): Status enum (e.g., `ALARM_WLL`)
- DP 115 (`WATERMODE`): Operation mode

A quirk handler is required to expose the water level sensors, binary sensors (alarms), and configuration entities.

